<title>FRANCE: Blast hits Corsica ferry company, no casualties.</title>
<headline>Blast hits Corsica ferry company, no casualties.</headline>
<dateline>AJACCIO, Corsica 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bomb damaged the offices of the ferry company running services between the French Mediterranean island of Corsica and the mainland, but no one was injured, police said on Friday.</p>
<p>Police said no one had claimed responsibility for the blast at the SNCM company offices in Bastia in northern Corsica.</p>
<p>Corsican separatists have attacked the company in the past as one of there targets in their campaign for increased autonomy from mainland France.</p>
</text>
